  "worked_solution": "A point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface has the corresponding position vector given by\n\n$$\nr=\u27e8x,\\,y,\\,z\u27e9=\u27e8x,\\,y,\\,(x+y)^{4}\u27e9.\n$$\n\nNow, setting $x=u$ and $y=v,$ we obtain a vector function that parametrizes the surface:\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=\u27e8u,\\,v,\\,(u+v)^{4}\u27e9\n$$",
